  "worked_solution": "The polar curve defined by the equation $\\theta =\\frac{23\\pi }{18}$ is the ray that starts at the origin and makes a counterclockwise angle of $\\frac{23\\pi }{18}$ with the positive $x$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the angle it makes with the negative $x$-axis is  \n\n$$\n\\frac{23\\pi }{18}-\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{18}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe correct answer is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/eadf7386a731c02931fc79d16d28d788c53917aa363100b32b4b2e9ec68db123.png)",
